<https://example.org/dmo/id/recommendation/a1c-test> a dmo:Recommendation ;
    rdfs:label "A1C test" ;
    dmo:recommendationId "a1c-test" ;
    dmo:recommendationStrength "Unspecified" ;
    dmo:recommendationType "Screening" ;
    dmo:statement "The A1C test is sometimes called the hemoglobin A1C, HbA1c, glycated hemoglobin, or glycohemoglobin test." ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "The A1C test is sometimes called the hemoglobin A1C, HbA1c, glycated hemoglobin, or glycohemoglobin test." ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "Screening and diagnosis of prediabetes1" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "Screening and diagnosis of type 2 diabetes1" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "repeat for confirmation of diagnosis" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "Diagnosis requires a laboratory test certified by the NGSP and standardized to the DCCT assay." ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "Some point-of-care A1C assays may be certified by the NGSP or approved by the U.S. Food and Drug Administration for diagnosis; however, they should only be considered in laboratories that are certified to perform moderate-to-high complexity tests to ensure testing proficiency." ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "Not recommended for rapidly progressing diabetes, e.g., type 1 diabetes in children1" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "Not recommended for screening cystic fibrosis NIH external link-related diabetes1" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "Because of these variations in test results, health care professionals should repeat tests before making a diagnosis." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/niddk-diabetes-prediabetes-tests> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/recommendation/confirming-diagnosis-of-type-2-diabetes-and-prediabetes> a dmo:Recommendation ;
    rdfs:label "Confirming diagnosis of type 2 diabetes and prediabetes" ;
    dmo:recommendationId "confirming-diagnosis-of-type-2-diabetes-and-prediabetes" ;
    dmo:recommendationStrength "Unspecified" ;
    dmo:recommendationType "Diagnosis" ;
    dmo:statement "Diagnosis of type 2 diabetes is definitively made by blood tests. Diagnosis requires two abnormal test results from the same sample or from two different samples. Repeat the test using one of the following methods: Repeat the same test or run a different test.1 The second test should be done immediately.1 If two test results indicate diabetes, consider the diagnosis confirmed.1 If the two different tests conflict, repeat the test that is above the diagnostic threshold. Diagnosis is made based on the confirmed test.1" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "Diagnosis of type 2 diabetes is definitively made by blood tests. Diagnosis requires two abnormal test results from the same sample or from two different samples. Repeat the test using one of the following methods Repeat the same test or run a different test.1 The second test should be done immediately.1 If two test results indicate diabetes, consider the diagnosis confirmed.1 If the two different tests conflict, repeat the test that is above the diagnostic threshold. Diagnosis is made based on the confirmed test.1" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/niddk-diabetes-prediabetes-tests> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/recommendation/considering-interference-in-a1c-test> a dmo:Recommendation ;
    rdfs:label "Considering interference in A1C test" ;
    dmo:recommendationId "considering-interference-in-a1c-test" ;
    dmo:recommendationStrength "Unspecified" ;
    dmo:recommendationType "Diagnosis" ;
    dmo:statement "consider the possibility of interference in the A1C test when a result is below 4%, above 15%, or is at odds with other diabetes test results1" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "consider the possibility of interference in the A1C test when a result is below 4%, above 15%, or is at odds with other diabetes test results1" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/niddk-diabetes-prediabetes-tests> .

